+> Dated note 2026-11-20 (M-246, prior text kept; FIX.CONFIG-BOUNDS · task-395 · lane BL-CFGBOUNDS; operator, verbatim: "yes follow the rules register them.", `~/Buildo-scratch/queues-20261113/MORNING-DECISIONS.md:1494`, answering whether page settings with bounds in the page schema are acceptable or must be registered). **Rule 3 is followed as written.** The six phone page settings (the search typing pause, the shortest search, the report-count freshness, the lookup retries, the lookup freshness and the semi page Continue wait) are registered logic variables, rows `maxbld_page_<key>` in `scripts/seeds/logic_variables.json` (a value, `min`, `max`, a stated `on_invalid`, a why). A surface declares each in the schema's existing field `config.logic_variables` (`name`, `min`, `max`, `on_invalid`, `why`); the schema refuses a number with no entry (the one validator `surface-validate` runs), and the mobile generator (`scripts/surfaces/emit-mobile-surfaces.mjs`) resolves each slice number from its seed row, refusing a mismatch or an out-of-range value. The phone reader `mobile/src/lib/sliceConfig.ts` applies the slice bounds (clamp warns, fail throws). The earlier grounder resolution (bounds in the surface schema, no database row) is superseded by these words. Values did not change. The bounds are declared for both platforms; only the phone applies them at run time, and no web binding reads these keys today.
